{"paper": "2025-Tier1-19-Sep-2025-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "letter-sequence", "splitter": "qn", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 93, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Two tangents are drawn from point P to a circle such that the angle between them is 80°. Find the angle between the radii at the points of contact.", "options": [{"text": "80°", "added": false}, {"text": "100°", "added": false}, {"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "110°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 2, "text": "Sector A has a radius of 4 cm and an angle of 60°. Sector B has a radius of 8 cm and an angle of 15°. Find the ratio of the area of Sector A to Sector B.", "options": [{"text": "1:1", "added": false}, {"text": "2:1", "added": false}, {"text": "1:2", "added": false}, {"text": "3:4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 3, "text": "If cos 𝜃 = y, express sin⁡2 𝜃 in terms of y.", "options": [{"text": "1 − 𝑦 2", "added": false}, {"text": "𝑦 2 − 1", "added": false}, {"text": "1 + 𝑦 2", "added": false}, {"text": "√1 − 𝑦 2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 4, "text": "A sum of money triples itself in 8 years at simple interest. In how many years will it become 7 times itself at the same interest rate?", "options": [{"text": "18 years", "added": false}, {"text": "24 years", "added": false}, {"text": "20 years", "added": false}, {"text": "16 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 5, "text": "P and Q are hired for a project for ₹1200. P starts the work alone; Q joins when 20% of the work is completed. If Q is 1.5 times as efficient as P, calculate Q's total earnings.", "options": [{"text": "₹500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹720", "added": false}, {"text": "₹576", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 6, "text": "If tan 𝜃 = 1, find the value of (1 + sin 𝜃)(1 - cos 𝜃). 1", "options": [{"text": "2 2−√2", "added": false}, {"text": "2 1", "added": false}, {"text": "4 1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 7, "text": "From an external point M, a tangent MT is drawn to a circle with center O. If OT = 8 cm and OM = 17 cm, find the area of the circle.", "options": [{"text": "64𝜋cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "225𝜋 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "289𝜋 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "49𝜋 cm²", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 8, "text": "If the exterior angle of a regular polygon is 24°, how many sides does the polygon have?", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "polygons", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 9, "text": "Simplify the expression: − √5−√3 √5+√3", "options": [{"text": "√3", "added": false}, {"text": "√5", "added": false}, {"text": "2√3", "added": false}, {"text": "2√5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 10, "text": "A large sphere of radius K is recast into m identical small spheres of radius k. The value of m is: 𝐾3", "options": [{"text": "𝑘 3 3𝐾", "added": false}, {"text": "𝑘 𝐾2", "added": false}, {"text": "𝑘 2 4𝐾 3", "added": false}, {"text": "𝑘 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 11, "text": "Evaluate: 0.93 +0.093 1", "options": [{"text": "9 1", "added": false}, {"text": "27 1", "added": false}, {"text": "3 1", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 12, "text": "When the square of a positive number is subtracted from 2531 and the resulting value is divided by 11, the quotient is 221. What is the number?", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "quadratic-equations", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 13, "text": "If cos⁡ 𝐴 + sin⁡ 𝐴 = √2cos⁡ 𝐴, 𝑡ℎ𝑒𝑛cos⁡ 𝐴 − sin⁡ 𝐴 is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "√2sin⁡ 𝐴", "added": false}, {"text": "sin 𝐴", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "√2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 14, "text": "A pole of length L casts a shadow on the ground. A wire is stretched from the top of the pole to the tip of the shadow making a 60° angle with the ground. If the pole is 12 meters high, find the length of the wire (approximate).", "options": [{"text": "10 m", "added": false}, {"text": "18 m", "added": false}, {"text": "16 m", "added": false}, {"text": "14 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "heights-and-distances", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 15, "text": "If 𝑥 + 𝑥 = −2, find the value of 𝑥 8 + 𝑥 8 + 2𝑥 5 + 𝑥 5 + 𝑥 2 + 𝑥 2 .", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "-2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 16, "text": "In △ PQR, PS is the bisector of ∠ QPR meeting QR at S. If PQ = PR, then △ PQS ≅△ PRS by which congruence criterion?", "options": [{"text": "SSS", "added": false}, {"text": "ASA", "added": false}, {"text": "SAS", "added": false}, {"text": "RHS", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": "c"}, {"n": 17, "text": "Which of the following coordinates satisfies the linear equation 2x - 3y = 6 ?", "options": [{"text": "(3, 0)", "added": false}, {"text": "(0, -2)", "added": false}, {"text": "(6, 2)", "added": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Coordinate Geometry", "sub": "distance-and-section", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 18, "text": "A shopkeeper marked an item 50% above the cost price and gave a 10% discount on the marked price. If the final selling price was ₹540, find the cost price.", "options": [{"text": "₹350", "added": false}, {"text": "₹400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹450", "added": false}, {"text": "₹380", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "b"}, {"n": 19, "text": "A total of ₹2200 is invested in three parts at 1%, 2%, and 3% per annum simple interest respectively. If the interest earned from each part after one year is equal, what is the sum invested at 3%?", "options": [{"text": "₹600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 20, "text": "Identify the correct statement(s):𝑖)√15 > 3.8𝑖𝑖)√17 > √15𝑖𝑖𝑖)√20 > √19", "options": [{"text": "i and ii", "added": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "added": false}, {"text": "i only", "added": false}, {"text": "i, ii and iii", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 21, "text": "If (a + b) : (a – b) = 7 : 3, find (𝑎2 + 𝑏2 ): (𝑎2 –𝑏2 )= ?", "options": [{"text": "29:21", "added": false}, {"text": "58:42", "added": false}, {"text": "31:25", "added": false}, {"text": "17:13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 22, "text": "A solid metal cylinder has a radius of 6 cm and a height of 14 cm. A hole of radius 2 cm is bored through the center along the axis. Find the volume of the remaining metal.", "options": [{"text": "1408 cm³", "added": false}, {"text": "1232 cm³", "added": false}, {"text": "1540 cm³", "added": false}, {"text": "1760 cm³", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 23, "text": "A water reservoir is 20 m long, 15 m wide, and 4 m deep. Determine its capacity in kilolitres.", "options": [{"text": "1,000 kL", "added": false}, {"text": "1,800 kL", "added": false}, {"text": "1,500 kL", "added": false}, {"text": "1,200 kL", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "d"}, {"n": 24, "text": "From point X outside a circle, tangent XY and secant XAB are drawn. If XY = 8 cm and XA = 4 cm, find the length of the chord AB.", "options": [{"text": "12 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "16 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "10 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "a"}, {"n": 25, "text": "A cone of height 12 cm is sliced by two planes parallel to the base at heights of 4 cm and 8 cm from the vertex. Find the ratio of the volumes of the three resulting sections (top:middle:bottom).", "options": [{"text": "1:7:19", "added": false}, {"text": "1:8:27", "added": false}, {"text": "8:19:37", "added": false}, {"text": "1:26:64", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": "a"}]}